==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Let's Go! Akane''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Akane is situational at the best of times. She is a bona fide [[Dodge Attack|Dodge]]-based tank who can [[Attacks Only|Only Attack]] [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] To put it bluntly, her crowd-control is mediocre, and she has a dreadfully long foreswing animation to go with it. The 50% activation rate on her [[Freeze]] pairs poorly with its ~57% uptime, to the point where you might as well disregard that she has it most of the time. Her DPS is equally abysmal when comparing her to other [[:Category:Focused Target Cats|units with the Attacks Only ability]].

Her main selling point is well and truly gambling. Akane has a very high base HP alongside a 60% chance to Dodge Attacks for 1 second. To Dodge Attacks with such a high activation rate can be comically broken in the right circumstances, as with units like [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] being capable of walling off even the most powerful [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] threats for minutes at a time. The main advantage of Dodge tanks is the potential to wall off entire armies continuously, as units like this seldom get overwhelmed by sheer numbers alone, especially since they're not outright tanking the brunt of their DPS. However, the ability is ultimately RNG-dependent, and can vary in performance greatly when compared to ordinary tanks like [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]]. Enemies who utilize slow, but consistently powerful attacks, tend to rip massive portions off her without giving Dodge the opportunity to even activate. For this reason, her best use cases are against fast attackers with low DPH that can repeatedly trigger her abilities and keep them active, that way, the stronger enemies will squander their attacks on an Akane who's in the middle of Dodging. Enemies like [[Professor A.]], [[Red EnerG]], [[Shadow Boxer K]], and even [[Poultrio]] are all good examples of enemies that will inadvertently protect her.

Where Akane really struggles is at the presence of anything she doesn't target, since all she can do to object is politely ask the enemies not to kill her. As a tanker who relies exclusively on Dodge to make up a majority of her survivability, any dangerous non-target pushers or peons will spell her doom if given the opportunity to run amok, so she's very high-maintenance to keep alive if a stage doesn't feature exclusively Red and/or Dark enemies (which most don't). Additionally, despite having a higher-than-average base HP, it is still not enough for her to facetank large hordes of target traits reliably for extended periods of time. She's expensive too, which only compounds with the rest of her problems. Overall, not a good Uber.

