==Trivia==
*Akane Tounji first became obtainable in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]] on August 8th, 2026.
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Akane Tounji's description misspelt neighborhood as "neighboorhood".
*Akane is a female Japanese name meaning "[[wikipedia:Rubiaceae|madder]]" (especially the [[wikipedia:Rubia cordifolia|Indian madder]] or [[wikipedia:Rubia argyi|Japanese madder]]), "madder red", or red dye made from madder. This may reference her [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] target and the partial red coloration of her Evolved Form's mech suit.
*[[wikipedia:ja:東雲寺|Tōun-ji]] (東雲寺) is the name of many temples in Japan.
*The word 鉄腕 ''tetsuwan'' in Akane Tounji's Japanese name means "strong arm", but literally translates to "iron arm", referencing Akane's use of a mech suit.
*Let's Go! Akane's name may be a reference to the anime ''[[wikipedia: Anpanman#Anime|Soreike! Anpanman]]'' (それいけ!アンパンマン, "Let's Go! Anpanman").
*Let's Go! Akane's maid outfit could possibly be a nod to [[Cat Maid (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Maid]], [[THE DYNAMITES (Gacha Event)|THE DYNAMITES]]' original [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou|VIP Uber Rare]].
*The term [[wikipedia:86 (term)|86]] in Let's Go! Akane's English description refers to kicking out someone from an establishment.

